{"version":1,"reference":{"kind":"artifact_content","namespace":"#408","artifact_type":"_dh-work-item-head-v1","name":"head"},"owner_reference":"#408","content":"{\"version\":1,\"issue_reference\":\"#408\",\"parent_revision\":\"9c324929b091f6c20912810c14c845e0d7c84ebe\",\"root_revision\":\"c570c3a23735ce06520dee30a4078d9d79caa9c1533b2afcae5bcdb9ab091ed0\",\"body\":\"<!-- backlog-metadata:\\npriority: P1\\ntype: Bug\\nstatus: open\\nadded: 2026-08-12\\n-->\\n\\n## Description\\n\\nThe implementation_manager.py TaskStatus enum only has 3 values: NOT_STARTED, IN_PROGRESS, COMPLETE. When a task is intentionally deferred (e.g., [DEFERRED] in title, status: not-started), the automation treats it as an incomplete task. This prevents /complete-implementation from triggering because the status check sees remaining NOT_STARTED tasks. Observed on issue #367 where 3/3 non-deferred tasks were COMPLETE but the deferred task kept the issue open. Need to add DEFERRED (and possibly SKIPPED, WONTFIX) as valid terminal statuses that count as \\\"done\\\" for completion gating. Affected files: plugins/python3-development/skills/implementation-manager/scripts/implementation_manager.py (TaskStatus enum, status parsing, ready-tasks logic, completion check), plugins/python3-development/skills/implementation-manager/scripts/task_format.py (YAML format support).\\n\\n## Acceptance Criteria\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n- [ ] Work matches description\\n- [ ] Plan or implementation complete\\n</div>\\n\\n## Story\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\nAs a **developer relying on this plugin**, I want to **fix: implementation manager lacks deferred/skipped task status \u2014 blocks auto-completion of task plans with intentionally deferred tasks** so that **the tool works correctly and reliably**.\\n</div>\\n\\n## Context\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n- **Source**: Session observation \u2014 issue #367 auto-close failure analysis (2026-03-03)\\n- **Priority**: P1\\n- **Added**: 2026-03-03\\n- **Research questions**: None\\n</div>\\n\\n## Groomed (2026-04-02)\\n\\n### Priority\\n\\n8/10 \u2014 A deferred task that is intentionally never run blocks /complete-implementation from triggering, requiring manual intervention for every plan that uses deferral. Confirmed live on issue #367 where 3/3 active tasks were COMPLETE but one DEFERRED task prevented auto-close.\\n\\n### Impact\\n\\n- Blocks: any SAM plan author who uses DEFERRED or SKIPPED tasks as intentional scope boundaries\\n- Bottleneck: /complete-implementation cannot be reached automatically when a plan contains deferred tasks, forcing human override or manual file edits\\n\\n### Benefits\\n\\n- SAM plans with intentionally deferred tasks complete automatically without human intervention\\n- DEFERRED and SKIPPED become first-class terminal statuses in the completion gate, consistent with the dependency-satisfaction logic already in the codebase\\n\\n### Expected Behavior\\n\\nWhen all non-deferred tasks in a plan reach COMPLETE, and the remaining tasks carry DEFERRED or SKIPPED status, the plan is considered fully resolved and /complete-implementation triggers automatically. The sam_status command reports 100% completion when all tasks are in any terminal status (COMPLETE, DEFERRED, or SKIPPED), not only when all are COMPLETE.\\n\\n### Desired Structure\\n\\nThe completion gate in implement-feature and the completion_pct calculation in get_plan_status both treat COMPLETE, DEFERRED, and SKIPPED as equivalent terminal states for the purpose of \\\"all tasks done\\\" evaluation. The prose in the Completion Gate section of implement-feature/SKILL.md reflects this. No task with a terminal status (any of the three) blocks auto-completion.\\n\\n### Acceptance Criteria\\n\\n1. Running `sam_status` on a plan where all tasks are COMPLETE, DEFERRED, or SKIPPED (in any combination) returns `completion_pct` of 100.0\\n2. Running `sam_ready` on a plan where all tasks are in terminal status returns an empty ready_tasks list and count=0\\n3. The implement-feature skill Completion Gate triggers when `sam_status` shows no NOT_STARTED or IN_PROGRESS tasks remain (not only when all show COMPLETE)\\n4. A task with `[DEFERRED]` in its title and status `not-started` is parsed as TaskStatus.DEFERRED by both implementation_manager.py and the SAM MCP server\\n5. The `get_plan_status` function in sam_schema/core/query.py counts DEFERRED and SKIPPED tasks in the terminal total, so a 4-task plan with 3 COMPLETE and 1 DEFERRED returns completion_pct=100.0\\n6. Existing tests for ready-task and dependency logic continue to pass\\n\\n### Resources\\n\\n| Type | Item |\\n|------|------|\\n| Prior work | plugins/development-harness/skills/implementation-manager/scripts/implementation_manager.py \u2014 TaskStatus enum at line 73, _TERMINAL_STATUSES at line 109, _status_from_title at line 405 (already correct) |\\n| Prior work | plugins/development-harness/sam_schema/core/models.py \u2014 TaskStatus enum at line 49, DEFERRED/SKIPPED at lines 56-57 (already correct) |\\n| Prior work | plugins/development-harness/sam_schema/core/dependencies.py \u2014 TERMINAL_STATUSES at line 15 includes DEFERRED and SKIPPED (already correct) |\\n| Prior work | plugins/development-harness/sam_schema/core/query.py \u2014 get_plan_status() at line 422; completion_pct at line 451 only counts COMPLETE (the gap) |\\n| Prior work | plugins/development-harness/skills/implement-feature/SKILL.md \u2014 Completion Gate at line 157: says \\\"When all tasks show COMPLETE\\\" (prose gap) |\\n| Prior work | plugins/development-harness/skills/implementation-manager/scripts/task_format.py \u2014 YAML status mapping at lines 31-32 |\\n| Backlog | #257 development-harness: Task Status MCP (related P1, same domain) |\\n\\n### Dependencies\\n\\n- Depends on: None \u2014 the sam_schema enum and dependency logic already have DEFERRED/SKIPPED; this fix is self-contained\\n- Blocks: #257 (Task Status MCP) may share overlapping scope; coordinate to avoid duplicate changes\\n\\n### Effort\\n\\nSmall \u2014 Two localized changes: (1) fix completion_pct in get_plan_status() in sam_schema/core/query.py to count all terminal statuses, (2) update the Completion Gate prose in implement-feature/SKILL.md to say \\\"When all tasks are in a terminal status (COMPLETE, DEFERRED, or SKIPPED)\\\" instead of \\\"When all tasks show COMPLETE\\\". The underlying enum, status parsing, and dependency logic are already correct.\\n\",\"digest\":\"d48188231deba53652cacbabf471fb23ed9e36e6c7a8067d5926b06341630541\",\"comment_id\":\"IC_kwDOQGimCs8AAAABPg1Blw\"}"}